      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0011",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Therefore, the performance of the [`addElement(_:boundingRectMin:boundingRectMax:splitStrategy:)`](gkrtree/addelement(_:boundingrectmin:boundingrectmax:splitstrategy:).md) method is faster (on average, across many calls).",
      "normalizedSource": "Therefore, the performance of the [`addElement(_:boundingRectMin:boundingRectMax:splitStrategy:)`](gkrtree/addelement(_:boundingrectmin:boundingrectmax:splitstrategy:).md) method is faster (on average, across many calls).",
      "sourceHash": "2060dfbe001dcdbc64f1cac61f23568ddebb8fecdf60b6d9585e6717b74a6cf8",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "A larger `maxNumberOfChildren` value means that the tree reorganizes itself less often.",
      "contextAfter": "But because each node contains a larger number of elements, the performance of the [`elements(inBoundingRectMin:rectMax:)`](gkrtree/elements(inboundingrectmin:rectmax:).md) method is slower (on average).",
